{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517692-charms-gadgets","id":1517692,"title":"Charms/Gadgets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-11T05:39:21-07:00","id":1517692,"title":"Charms/Gadgets","content":"In Forged by Dragon Fire, Charms were simple wonders that held and effect in an item. You roll Arete at creation (meaning you can stack successes) and anyone can use it (as long as the paradigm fit).<br /> <br /> Now, in Book of Secrets, it seems now that charms have an Arete trait that must be rolled during activation, which will determine how powerful is the result.<br /> To me, this alone is a big nerf that makes charms nearly useless. The big thing about charms were to have potent and quick, yet expendable, effect. <br /> So, apart from allowing other people to use the effect, and be able to use 2 effects in a turn, I don't see any advantage of charms as ruled in BoS.<br /> <br /> The creation requires 5 quintessence per lvl of the wonder and a lot of successes. And It's not a fast process to do.<br /> <br /> Also, despite BoS saying that Charms/Gadgets have an Arete trait that should be rolled *none* of the charms/gadgets provided as examples have this trait.<br /> <br /> So, what you guys think about that and which rule do you use in your table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T06:28:12-07:00","id":1517694,"title":"","content":"Well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BoS. p.140</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">System-wise, each Charm is a mystic Effect that has been \u201cheld\u201d in time until a certain activity sets the magick free. Essentially, such items contain a delayed-action spell. For that reason, <b>a Charm does <u>not</u> require an Arete roll</b>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>also BoS. p.140</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>To activate a Charm, the player who\u2019s using the Charm rolls the Arete of that Charm</b>, against difficulty 7. The number of successes determines the strength of the Effect ... goes on to present a system on how this works\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Normaly I would think the first sentence was a typo, since the section goes on to explain how, in fact, Charms have an Arete and you roll it. But then, the example Charm says you roll 5 dice of damage - that can't be modeled by having Arete (as it would give 2+1 success on the damage table, that can never be equivalent to 5 dice). And it says Arete: N/A - explicitly. And the book hasn't any rule to determine the Arete of Charms based on value<br /> <br /> Since the book contradicts itsef so easily, and doesn't care about following or supporting it's own rule, I would say: Go with whatever you think it's best.<br /> <br /> It seems that the idea was to employ a new system, but, as always seems to be the case with Wonders, it fails to actually make it work as a consistent mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-11-2023, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T07:10:25-07:00","id":1517699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517692-charms-gadgets?p=1517694#post1517694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Normaly I would think the first sentence was a typo, since the section goes on to explain how, in fact, Charms have an Arete and you roll it. But then, the example Charm says you roll 5 dice of damage - that can't be modeled by having Arete (as it would give 2+1 success on the damage table, that can never be equivalent to 5 dice). And it says Arete: N/A - explicitly. And the book hasn't any rule to determine the Arete of Charms based on value<br /> <br /> Since the book contradicts itsef so easily, and doesn't care about following or supporting it's own rule, I would say: Go with whatever you think it's best.<br /> <br /> It seems that the idea was to employ a new system, but, as always seems to be the case with Wonders, it fails to actually make it work as a consistent mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's pretty confusing and contradicting. One could argue that it doesn't require an Arete roll from the user. But that is not what is written. Also, it's pretty.clear by the examples and the description (effect held in time) that the roll has been made at creation.<br /> <br /> I hate those contradictions. Anyway, I think that 5 quint per dot is a very expensive price to pay, so if you can't roll Arete at creation (stacking) then it is simply not worth it at all.<br /> <br /> I will probably use FbDG rules, that are way more solid. What is your take, or your table's, on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T08:05:12-07:00","id":1517702,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I use FbDG rules. Which it seems to be what's being reffered to at the beggining with the whole &quot;effect held in time&quot; thing: Much likeTime 4 triggers, but less costly in terms of personal power/knowledge needed (2-3 Prime instead of Time 4), and more costly in terms of resources employed.<br /> <br /> I think that's pretty reasonable in terms of cost-beneffit and balance. Also I like that Spheres can be used to &quot;mimick&quot; other spheres, altrough with different levels of efficiency and metaphisical implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T09:17:08-07:00","id":1517705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517692-charms-gadgets?p=1517702#post1517702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I use FbDG rules. Which it seems to be what's being reffered to at the beggining with the whole &quot;effect held in time&quot; thing: Much likeTime 4 triggers, but less costly in terms of personal power/knowledge needed (2-3 Prime instead of Time 4), and more costly in terms of resources employed.<br /> <br /> I think that's pretty reasonable in terms of cost-beneffit and balance. Also I like that Spheres can be used to &quot;mimick&quot; other spheres, altrough with different levels of efficiency and metaphisical implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I was thinking if there were more differences between charms and Time trigger other then the ones you posted. Charms can be activated by any trigger as well, right? You dont have to destroy or consume the item.<br /> <br /> Also, the cost changed too. In BoS they merged the cost to all wonders as 5 quint per dot. FbDF has a cos of 1 per dot, iirc. At least for charms, I don't remember the other wonders. I find 5 quint for a lvl 1 effect that you'll use a few times expensive as fuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T10:12:18-07:00","id":1517706,"title":"","content":"Well, that depends on how common or rare it's Quintessence on the setting. If a lvl 1 Node can give me one &quot;batch&quot; of ghost-sensing candles a week, it's worth it. If I, so to speak, have to ask Porthos to lend me a Node each time I want to make them, then it's too expensive.<br /> <br /> AFAIK there's no mandatory need to consume the item, altrough the option lends very naturally to consumables","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T19:55:02-07:00","id":1517734,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">System-wise, each Charm is a mystic Effect that has been \u201cheld\u201d in time until a certain activity sets the magick free. Essentially, such items contain s delayed-action spell. For that reason, a Charm does not require an Arete roll, and anyone who believes in such things can use one.</div> <br /> I read this as saying that Charms don't require the <i>user</i> to make an Arete roll. This doesn't contradict the next paragraph that says that the <i>Charm's</i> Arete needs to be rolled when the Effect is activated. Although the examples of Charms and Gadgets that <i>don't require Arete rolls at all</i> add a wrinkle to this: there seems to be an implicit \u201cif the Charm needs an Arete roll to determine how effective it is, <i>then</i> roll the Charm's Arete.\u201d An example of this is the Bond Fine Tobacco Products (p.159), which rolls four dice on a Mind 2 Effect to convince the smoker to trust the supplier. By contrast, Ectoplasmic Disruption Rounds don't need to make any roll at all: chamber the round and pull the trigger, and even if your target is an unmanifested spirit, you can damage it. (It also says that it's especially effective against vampires and werewolves, though it doesn't say what the game system for this is. My own house role is that the damage is treated as aggravated for them, whereas it's merely lethal for anyone else. But I'm rambling; getting back on topic:<br /> <br /> The benefit of a Charm or Gadget is that you never make just one: the prices for them are <i>per batch</i>. You don't get one cigarette; you get a pack of twenty. You don't get one bullet; you get a clip of ten. You don't get one Energy Drink; you get a six-pack of them. You don't get <i>a</i> Ginger Dragon; you get a <i>bag</i> of them.<br /> <br /> The creation rules say that the batch size is twice the crafter's Arete; and since creating a Charm requires at least Prime 2, that means that the minimum batch size is four. Five Quintessence per batch isn't so bad when it's split over four Charms in that batch; and it can be downright cheap if the Crafter has Arete 5 and therefore is splitting the energy cost over ten Charms. That's one Quintessence for every <i>two</i> dots per individual Charm.<br /> <br /> By contrast, the Background rules for Charms say that the batch size is 10. Presumably, you adjust the Background cost accordingly if you bundle up your Charms in other quantities: the aforementioned six-pack of energy drinks ought to cost 6/10 as much as other Charms as a Background, because each pack of only giving you six uses instead of the normal ten. Conversely, the pack of twenty cigarettes should cost twice as much as a Background because you get twice as many uses out of it compared to the normal ten uses.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's largely a moot point if you're not charging experience points for Backgrounds. The RAW assume that you are; but I see no reason why this <i>must</i> be the case. If the Storyteller chooses <i>not</i> to charge xp for Charms, though, it's up to him to regulate their availability in the game. Which can potentially be tricky.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-12-2023, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T07:30:08-07:00","id":1517767,"title":"","content":"To be honest, &quot;does not require an Arete roll&quot; is differente from &quot;does not require an Arete roll from the user&quot;. The first implies no roll at all.Also, the &quot;held in time&quot; and &quot;delayed action&quot; implies that the spell is cast beforehand, just like in FbDF. And then they go on and explain how you have to roll the charm Arete. M20 wonder system is a shit show.<br /> <br /> Even considering batches, why would you spend 5 quint *per dot of charm* (so, your Arete 5 master would create 10 lvl 3 charms, by paying 15 quint.) for an effect that you can cast yourself? With the exact same dice pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T08:18:20-07:00","id":1517776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517692-charms-gadgets?p=1517767#post1517767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, &quot;does not require an Arete roll&quot; is differente from &quot;does not require an Arete roll from the user&quot;. The first implies no roll at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, my reading of it is that \u201cdoes not require an Arete roll from the user\u201d was the intent, and the way it was written was poorly phrased. Brucato isn't good at technical writing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517692-charms-gadgets?p=1517767#post1517767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the &quot;held in time&quot; and &quot;delayed action&quot; implies that the spell is cast beforehand, just like in FbDF. And then they go on and explain how you have to roll the charm Arete.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you've said. The problem with that is that there are strict limitations as to what \u201ccasting beforehand\u201d can do. In many cases (three out of the four sample Charms/Gadgets), that's sufficient, and no Arete roll is needed when activating it. But in some cases, the Effect needs to interact with aspects of the environment that the crafter of the Charm cannot predict; such is the case for the cigarettes. In <i>those</i> cases, rolling ahead of time doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying that every Charm has to have an Arete roll; only that some do, and when it does, you roll the Charm's Arete, not the user's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517692-charms-gadgets?p=1517767#post1517767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even considering batches, why would you spend 5 quint *per dot of charm* (so, your Arete 5 master would create 10 lvl 3 charms, by paying 15 quint.) for an effect that you can cast yourself? With the exact same dice pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a \u201cproblem\u201d with Wonders <i>in general</i>. Why make a Talisman, or an Artifact, or, yes, a Charm, when you can just perform the Effect yourself?<br /> <br /> Part of the solution is that activating a Wonder is often easier than performing an Effect yourself. You don't need any of your own Instruments to use a Wonder; you just need a Focus that's compatible with it. If your Instruments take time to use, this makes the Wonder faster, too. A mage with Mind 2 can work an Effect to get a mark to trust him; but that will require him to work with his Instruments in accordance with his Practice. And depending on the mage's Practice and Instruments and the situation at hand, that might be problematic.<br /> <br /> But the <i>other</i> part of the solution is that most Wonders can be used by <i>other people</i>. Talismans and Charms, in particular, aren't even restricted to use by <i>mages</i>. Those cigarettes can be given to an agent who doesn't have <i>any</i> Mind Magick, or even any Magick at all, and he'll be able to hand them out to marks and get the same benefits out of them. In fact, Charms aren't even restricted to Extraordinary Citizens: you could hand a pack of these cigarettes to a completely ordinary <i>Sleeper</i>, and instruct him to pass them out to his colleagues before the next board meeting; and that will work. And you need neither Time (to hang the Effect) nor Correspondence (to work the Effect when you're not present) in order to do so.<br /> <br /> I could see that being worth 1.5 Quintessence per cigarette.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-12-2023, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T18:46:59-07:00","id":1518800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517692-charms-gadgets?p=1517776#post1517776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you've said. The problem with that is that there are strict limitations as to what \u201ccasting beforehand\u201d can do. In many cases (three out of the four sample Charms/Gadgets), that's sufficient, and no Arete roll is needed when activating it. But in some cases, the Effect needs to interact with aspects of the environment that the crafter of the Charm cannot predict; such is the case for the cigarettes. In <i>those</i> cases, rolling ahead of time doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying that every Charm has to have an Arete roll; only that some do, and when it does, you roll the Charm's Arete, not the user's.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as &quot;you don't have to roll Arete&quot;. or you roll it beforehand im creation (which would allow for gathering sux) or you roll at activation.<br /> <br /> Even a simple +1 on an attribute like the Energy Drink should require an Arete roll (and thus an Arete stat). Afterall, you could always fail the roll...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517692-charms-gadgets?p=1517776#post1517776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a \u201cproblem\u201d with Wonders <i>in general</i>. Why make a Talisman, or an Artifact, or, yes, a Charm, when you can just perform the Effect yourself?<br /> <br /> Part of the solution is that activating a Wonder is often easier than performing an Effect yourself. You don't need any of your own Instruments to use a Wonder; you just need a Focus that's compatible with it. If your Instruments take time to use, this makes the Wonder faster, too. A mage with Mind 2 can work an Effect to get a mark to trust him; but that will require him to work with his Instruments in accordance with his Practice. And depending on the mage's Practice and Instruments and the situation at hand, that might be problematic.<br /> <br /> But the <i>other</i> part of the solution is that most Wonders can be used by <i>other people</i>. Talismans and Charms, in particular, aren't even restricted to use by <i>mages</i>. Those cigarettes can be given to an agent who doesn't have <i>any</i> Mind Magick, or even any Magick at all, and he'll be able to hand them out to marks and get the same benefits out of them. In fact, Charms aren't even restricted to Extraordinary Citizens: you could hand a pack of these cigarettes to a completely ordinary <i>Sleeper</i>, and instruct him to pass them out to his colleagues before the next board meeting; and that will work. And you need neither Time (to hang the Effect) nor Correspondence (to work the Effect when you're not present) in order to do so.<br /> <br /> I could see that being worth 1.5 Quintessence per cigarette.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand your point. However, the &quot;why create a wonder when you can just cast&quot; is even worse when the wonder gets wasted after used. <br /> <br /> If the author intention was to really get rid of accumulated successes Charms, I can't understand why...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}